Let's set things straight.  The sx164 uses a 21164PC aka pca56 cpu at
400 or 533 MHz.  The speed is set with some switches on the mother
board.  The only documented speeds are 400 and 533.  Setting one of
the remaining combinations gives 400 MHz.

Do not confuse sx164 with lx164 or rx164.  The lx164 uses an ev56 cpu,
up to 600 MHz (I think).  The rx164 uses a pca56 at up to 600 MHz.  Of
course, the 600 MHz cpu will work in an sx164, but only at 533 MHz.

