If you ever been to Samba.org you would be aware that it's pretty basic and
generally, when ever they have an update, the frontpage is renewed.

The speed claim was something I found sometime ago with a prior version.
That was about a year or so ago. What prompted them to make the statement
was simple, numerous people complained about the slow speed... If you want
to view some perf stats, take a look at:

http://setiathome.ssl.berkeley.edu/stats/team/team_89045.html

Keep in mind, if you go to the main page and check out stats sorted by cpu,
you will notice one glaring fact... The fastest Alphas process one Seti WU
in 20min... The FASTEST AMD/Intel are in the area of 3hrs... I 'think' the
fastest Alpha currently out, it something like 800mhz... I know there were
rumors about them releasing a 12000mhz model but I don't think that idea
ever bore fruit..

PS On the link I provided, please keep in mind that they're ALL running the
same text client version except for member #4, he's using the screen
saver... Also keep in mind, the versions for the i386 are optimized for
their respective cpu's wild the Alpha version isn't...


