Millennium
> > II, since these boxes came with that card too, or am I screwed? Is there
> > some way I can get the box to accept another graphics card?
>
>   Well, I'm not sure, but SRM is quite picky about which graphics card
> it accepts. From what I had heard it is possible to use Matrox cards,
> 3dfx Voodoo cards and some ATI cards.

This problem occurs when you have the Miata MX5 chipset. This chipset
is buggy so Digital locked the 64bit Slots and only tested cards have access
to the 64bit slots.
You can bypass this by typing:
>>> set pci_device_override [DEVICE_ID][VENDOR-ID]
Disabling the whole card checking:
>>> set pci_device_override -1
But the easiest way is to put the card in an other slot.




