that breaks it !!!
I've cross-posted because I'm not sure if this is Alpha specific.

I had 3 SCSI HD daisy chained on a NCRC875 and it worked OK.
Now I just tried to add another HD at the end of the chain, not ultrawide,
did it and I can't boot anymore. Fine, I remove it and still it won't boot,
even with only the main drive.

The SCSI config utility on boot tells me that my card and various drives are
enabled (HD on ID0, CD and JAZ on ID 6 and 7).

