Ben <Ben.Engbers@brouwercp.nl> wrote:
> 
> In the Netherlands, I have never heard of Qlogic SCSI-cards

Most likely any NCR 53C.... controller (a.k.a. Symbios, a.k.a.
Intraserver), with a possible exception of a newer 10xx cards and maybe
895/6, will also work with your SRM, it probably be cheaper,  and a
Linux driver for these cards is of a much better quality than the one
for Qlogic. 53C810 is not too speedy :-) but you will have to rummage
through some dusty corners to find one.

If your kernel has 'sym53c8xx_2' driver then this one preferred for
all those cards over older 'ncr53c8xx' and 'sym53c8xx' drivers
(the last one is not good for 810 and 810A, 'ncr53c8xx' will not
cover "high end", 'sym53c8xx_2' is fine for all of these).

> so even if
> I manage to find one, can I just install it in the machine and will it
> be recognized automatically or do I have to do something  special?

Nothing special.  Type 'show config | more' at SRM prompt and if your
firmware can work with an installed card it will show up in listings.

There are SRM variants which recognize Adaptec cards as well but
possibly not for your board.

  Michal


