>
>It probably has the pnp enabled. pnpdump reports nothing, but perhaps
>it's not supposed to.

Right, the 3c509 doesn't use the mechanism supported by pnpdump/isapnp
(which works without problems on my XL 266, too, BTW), but a proprietary
mechanism 3com invented becouse ISA-PnP wasn't invented at that time.

>I guess I could fit the card in a DOS machine and use the DOS tools to
>pick values for the IO etc.

You should take a look into /proc/ioports and /proc/interrupts beforehand to
find values not yet used in your system. I have found IRQ 11 to be used by
the on-board NCR, 15, 9, and 10 to be used by the 4 PCI slots (from system
board down), I couldn't get IRQ 12 (PS/2 mouse, but not connected) and IRQ
13 to work with ISA cards, I guess 14 wouldn't work either, as this'll be
the on-board IDE controller (can't remember if I tested this nonetheless).

So I use IRQ 5, 7 (parrallel port), and 3 (2nd serial port) for my three ISA
cards. This also means, I can't use the 2nd serial port and would I want to
use the parrallel port, I had to use polling.

IO-port-wise, I'm using 0x280-0x28f, 0x290-0x2f, and 0x300-0x30f, I didn't
try other ranges.

                             Right now, I'm connected through a 3c900
>(PCI), which works fine.

Or you go with that.

HTH, Bodo
